Let $A\subseteq V$ and let $f,g:V\to\mathbb R$ satisfy $g|_A=0$ and $f+g,f-g\in[-M,M]^V$. Set $$\nu=(\sigma_{f+g}^M)^{\mathrm{sym}}
       +(\sigma_{f-g}^M)^{\mathrm{sym}}.$$ Then, for every $z\in V$, $$\label{eq:launch-uncertainty}
 E_\nu(z\mid A)\geq2|g(z)|.$$ Moreover, for every $u,v\in V$, $$\label{eq:paired-separation}
 \begin{split}
 D_\nu(u,v)
 &=|f(u)-f(v)+g(u)-g(v)|\\
 &\quad+|f(u)-f(v)-g(u)+g(v)|
 \geq2|g(u)-g(v)|.
 \end{split}$$

Let a path of bags run from a bag containing $y$ to a later bag containing $z$.*


1.  *If an anchor $A$ lies on this path and its reservation lasts from $A$ through the later bag, then $$\label{eq:anchor-launch-test}
     D_{\mathrm{anc}}(y,z)\geq b_k d(z,A).$$*

2.  *Suppose a testing bag $P$ lies on the path and a reserved particle $F$ is unchanged from $P$ through the later bag. If, with probability at least $\theta$, it satisfies $$|F(z)-F(s)|\geq t\quad\text{for every }s\in P,$$ where $0<t\leq\operatorname{diam}(V)$, then $$\label{eq:anchor-height-test}
     D_{\mathrm{anc}}(y,z)\geq b_k\theta t.$$ In the second assertion the tested reservation and vertices are chosen without consulting launch randomness.*

*Both assertions allow the later bag to be the eviction bag.

For each fixed $k\geq2$ there is a constant $\lambda_k>0$ such that, for every admissible weighted graph with a tree decomposition of bag size at most $k$ and every pair of vertices $u,v$, $$\label{eq:combined-lower}
 D_{\mathrm{bag}}(u,v)+D_{\mathrm{anc}}(u,v)
 \geq\lambda_k d(u,v).$$
